   "text": "And why I'm telling you this, because most of the times we have seen that the moment you exactly reach out to the growth teams or the product teams or the founders of early stage startup or maybe well-settled companies as well, the first thing that they say, \"Okay, let's improve the design or the user experience.\" Sometimes a beautifully designed step also that does not need to be there is still a friction. So, it's not that only bad user design or bad user interface is a friction. Sometimes a good user interface also, which is not needed there, is also a friction, and might decrease your users or increase the churn rate. Now, the audit framework that we are talking about will not ask, \"Hey, is this step beautifully designed or not?\" We will see does this step even deserve to be this at this particular place right now or not? Or is it really needed to take a user towards the aha moment. 3 patterns of this friction added with the best of intentions. And if you recognize any of these in your teams, then the rest of this topic will actually fix all of them. The pattern 1, is the explanation first kind of steps. For example, welcome video, product tour of the main tool, the tooltip carousel that we exactly talked about. The team explains how everything works before letting the user do anything. Now, what happened is users, let's say, skip the explanations."
