   "text": "Now look at what every team typically reports at the end of a quarter, and this is what exactly I'm showing is how this works in real time in the real tech companies across the globe. You call it in India, US, Europe, Asia Pacific, it stays the same everywhere. Generally, marketing would be reporting the number of leads or the number of marketing qualified leads that they generated. So, marketing would report at, let's say, \"Hey, we delivered 4 times more marketing qualified leads or MQLs than the last year.\" Sales team would of course focus on the revenue, and they might say that, \"Hey, we have hit 105% of the target that was given to us.\" The customer success might say that, \"Hey, we retained 92% of the customers, so we did a pretty fair job.\" Renewal team might say is that, \"Hey, let's say 95% or like ninety percent of the amount got renewed.\" So, now if you look at from the team perspective, each team is hitting their numbers, and that's how the reporting also happens in the real companies. Where, let's say, if this particular reporting is happening in silos, every team, every or we That's why we say that every team of this, which is marketing, sales, customer success, renewal, every team is a revenue team or a revenue growth team. Now, if these teams are actually doing those in silos, it might feel that, hey, each team is winning, each team is celebrating quarterly. But now look at what the customer actually experiences."
