   "text": "This topic is about sales integration into your AARRR funnel, about where sales meets marketing. And this is one of the most important phase or the integral collaboration in any kind of successful company, where sales meet customer success, and where most of the growth dysfunction actually lives when the teams are not able to collaborate with each other and unable to generate that success on a company level instead of on a team level. Like let's say you may be successful in your marketing team or in your sales team or customer success team, but when all of them put together and when we look at the results, maybe on the company end, we are not able to generate that success. That's what we exactly want to solve here, because someone has to take a marketing qualified lead and turn it into a sales qualified lead. Someone has to take that closed one deal or the turned customer and turn it into an activated customer. Then there has to be someone in the company who has to take a renewing customer and turn them into an advocate or an ambassador for our company. Now, every one of those transitions is a handoff from one team to another team, and with its own rules, its own data, and its own failure modes as well that comes along with it naturally. Now, when a B2B company struggles to grow, generally what we have seen is that the problem is rarely inside any one team. In fact, it is between the functioning and the collaboration that has to go from one team to the another team."
