   "text": "Wherein if you talk about a billboard, it is not targeting anything. Whoever drives past to that location is the target. Now, the focus here is the narrower your ICP, the better targeting you will have, and your ads will perform better at a better unit economics. The second important factor is control. How much can you influence the outcome from that channel? For example, on LinkedIn ads or Google ads, you can choose your audience, you can choose your keyword, your budget, your ad creative. Wherein if you talk about on organic or word of mouth, you have much lesser control and lesser predictability. You cannot dial word of mouth up with a budget, or you can increase that. So, high control channel will give you predictability that, yes, if I increase this amount of budget or if I increase these five actions, then I can control the outcome here, and that's why I can predict what I can change with this particular action. But you have low control, then you'll not be able to predict that, okay, how much output I can get. If it works, how much it will work? We exactly don't know. The third factor is the input. I mean, what does it cost to run? And not just the ad amount we are talking about. What will the time it will take? What is the skills that we need? And do we need internal or external talent to run this specific channel? For example, an Instagram creator partnership would need a content team. SEO would need technical skill and content team again."
